It's not so much that -- it's that in the current code, the chance of
casting successfully is checked before you are prompted for a direction
(probably to save keystrokes for people failing to cast directional
spells).

Once you've passed that check, the spell is now definitely going to be
cast; your only choice is now "which direction", and the "energy is
released" stuff is just in-game rationalization for that.  (Part of this
is because you don't get into spell-specific code, such as determining
whether a direction is necessary, until much later, and there's no
functionality to pass back "user cancelled".  Rather than build it in,
it looks like TDT just added the 'magic is released' tidbit.)

